        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs(line): document responsePrefix",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`docs/channels/line.md` does not document the `responsePrefix` field, which is available for LINE via the inherited `ReplyRuntimeConfigSchemaShape`. Users configuring LINE cannot discover this feature from the docs.\n\n- Problem: The `responsePrefix` field exists in the LINE config schema but is absent from the docs\n- Solution: Add a `responsePrefix` mention to the Message behavior section of the LINE docs\n- What changed: `docs/channels/line.md` (+1 line in Message behavior)\n- What did NOT change: No code or behavior changes. Documentation only.\n\n**Documented field**:\n- **`responsePrefix`** (string) — optional string prepended to every outbound reply\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Schema — `responsePrefix` via `ReplyRuntimeConfigSchemaShape` (`src/config/zod-schema.core.ts:657`)\n\n```typescript\nresponsePrefix: z.string().optional(),\n```\n\nThe LINE config schema extends `LineCommonConfigSchemaBase` which spreads `ReplyRuntimeConfigSchemaShape`, inheriting `responsePrefix` alongside other reply-formatting fields.\n\n### LINE types (`extensions/line/src/types.ts:30`)\n\n```typescript\nresponsePrefix?: string;\n```\n\n### How `responsePrefix` is consumed at runtime\n\nThe LINE channel sends messages through `extensions/line/src/outbound.runtime.ts`, which passes the reply config (including `responsePrefix`) through the SDK`s shared outbound pipeline. The `responsePrefix` is prepended to the message text before the LINE API call. This path is shared by all channels that extend `ReplyRuntimeConfigSchemaShape`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can now discover the `responsePrefix` option from the LINE channel docs. This field was already functional — it was simply invisible to users who configure via docs.",
